    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d53-a2">

                <pb facs="0153" n="1113" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1113"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    305.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mariscal to Mr. Connery.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-02-18"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 18,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chargé d’affaires</hi>: I have just received your
                    note of this date, touching the notice you give of the arrest in Ventanas and
                    the conduct to Cosalá of the American Oliver Woods, on the charge of having
                    furnished corn to the bandit Eraclio Bernal.</p>
                <p>I at once communicated with the governors of the States of Sinaloa and Durango,
                    requesting, by telegraph, that in case the said Woods had been apprehended, they
                    should take care that he be tried under all the guaranties granted to the
                    accused by the constitution and the laws.</p>
                <p>I reiterate, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Igno. Mariscal</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
